  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment is low (≤0.33) and model shows upward bias, especially after recent spikes.",
    "Reduce forecast overshoots following sharp price spikes (e.g., >70.0) by 5-10% in the next 5-7 days.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias: if forecast is 5% above recent 7-day average, reduce by 1-2% per day until convergence.",
    "Increase forecast sensitivity to sentiment spikes: if sentiment >0.5, model should respond with 2-3% higher adjustment than baseline.",
    "Avoid over-optimism in early forecast windows (1-3 days) when sentiment is neutral or negative — use conservative baseline adjustments."
  ]
